From: dasher@netcom.com (Anton Sherwood)
Date: Wed, 30 Nov 1994 22:24:56 -0800
Subject: [#94-12-5] dumb barter

A couple of you have asked me what "dumb barter" means.  Here's how 
I understand it:  A trading ship lands on a strange shore.  The crew
sets out some goods on the beach, returns to the ship, and waits.
Natives come down, set out some goods of their own, and retreat to
cover to watch.  If the sea-people like what they see, they pick up
the natives' offering and split.  If not, they add to or subtract 
from their own offering, and repeat the cycle.  Eventually, one 
side accepts the offer by picking it up and departing.

In unrelated news, Phil Goetz asks:
> Why have a government?

Anyone feel qualified to answer that one?



